0\n  title: \"prd003-format R2.1-R2.4: FileTypeColor and color detection unit tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (color output requirements R2.1-R2.4)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (implementation under test -- FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/color_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, and ColorEnabled\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI escape sequence for all eight GNU ls file types (directory, symlink, executable, block device, char device, socket, pipe, regular) per prd003 R2.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled and empty string when color is disabled per prd003 R2.2\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test ColorEnabled returns false for non-*os.File io.Writer and performs TTY detection for *os.File per prd003 R2.3\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test that color constant values match GNU ls LS_COLORS defaults -- blue for directory, cyan for symlink, green for executable, yellow bold for block and char devices, magenta for socket, yellow for pipe per prd003 R2.4\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use SetColorEnabled(true) to force color on and SetColorEnabled(false) to force color off during tests, with defer ResetColorEnabled() for cleanup per prd003 R2.7 (designed for test teardown)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Test R2.3 automatic TTY detection by passing a non-terminal io.Writer (e.g., bytes.Buffer) to ColorEnabled to verify false return, and passing os.Stderr to exercise the *os.File TTY detection path\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Tests that call SetColorEnabled must not run in parallel with each other since colorOverride is process-global per prd003 R2.6\"\n\n 