{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":355392,"duration_api_ms":355343,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven pipeline that regenerates Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specifications, verifying parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform-divergent syscalls, `pkg/format/` handles shared output formatting, and `cmd/<utility>/` holds per-utility implementations. Magefiles bridge human-guided specification to automated synthesis.\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists on the working branch for `pkg/testutils/` (with tests), `pkg/format/` (no tests visible), and `pkg/sys/` (no tests visible). No `cmd/` packages have source code on this branch. Specs are complete for releases 00.0 through 04.1 (except 02.0–02.2 which are pending).\n\n**Current release**: Release 00.0 (foundational infrastructure) is the earliest incomplete release. Three of four use cases have implementation code present (`pkg/format`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/testutils`), but `pkg/format` and `pkg/sys` lack test files. `pkg/testutils` has both implementation and tests.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **Release 00.0** is earliest incomplete per P1\n2. Within 00.0: `pkg/format` and `pkg/sys` implementations exist but lack tests; `cmd/version` needs implementation\n3. Per P8 (libraries before consumers): library tests come before `cmd/version`\n4. Per P8 (alphabetical tiebreak): `color_test.go` < `column_test.go` < `size_test.go`, so color tests are first\n5. prd003-format R2.1–R2.4 is exactly 4 sub-requirements (the constraint limit), covering FileTypeColor, Reset, and ColorEnabled\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd003-format R2.1-R2.4: FileTypeColor and color detection unit tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (color output requirements R2.1-R2.4)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (implementation under test -- FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/color_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, and ColorEnabled\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI escape sequence for all eight GNU ls file types (directory, symlink, executable, block device, char device, socket, pipe, regular) per prd003 R2.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled and empty string when color is disabled per prd003 R2.2\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test ColorEnabled returns false for non-*os.File io.Writer and performs TTY detection for *os.File per prd003 R2.3\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test that color constant values match GNU ls LS_COLORS defaults -- blue for directory, cyan for symlink, green for executable, yellow bold for block and char devices, magenta for socket, yellow for pipe per prd003 R2.4\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use SetColorEnabled(true) to force color on and SetColorEnabled(false) to force color off during tests, with defer ResetColorEnabled() for cleanup per prd003 R2.7 (designed for test teardown)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Test R2.3 automatic TTY detection by passing a non-terminal io.Writer (e.g., bytes.Buffer) to ColorEnabled to verify false return, and passing os.Stderr to exercise the *os.File TTY detection path\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Tests that call SetColorEnabled must not run in parallel with each other since colorOverride is process-global per prd003 R2.6\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC